>> title: Yuenyeung
>> category: Drinks
>> tags: coffee, tea, hong kong, evaporated milk, drink
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: yuenyeung, yuen yeung, yuanyang, yin yong, 鴛鴦, coffee and tea, Coffee & Tea, coffee with tea, tea coffee mix, hong kong coffee tea, yin yeung
>> pairs-with: hong-kong-milk-tea
>> servings: 2
>> time: 15 min
>> step.1: steep 4 min, press it down
>> step.2: pour in two of tea to one of coffee
>> step.3: top up the milk, sugar to taste

Steep @ground dark roast coffee{2%Tbs}(11 g; coarse, for a press) in @boiling water{3/4%cup}(180 mL) in a #French press{} ~steep{4%min}, then press it down slowly.

Pour @Hong Kong milk tea{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL; hot, the recipe on this shelf) into @&(~1)coffee{}.

Stir @evaporated milk{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @granulated sugar{2%tsp}(to taste) through @&(~1)yuenyeung{} and pour it while it is still hot.
